  "instance_name": "anti_black_criminality_stereotype",
  "label": "Anti-Black Criminality Stereotype",
  "description": "A pervasive racial stereotype that associates Black people with criminal behavior, often used to justify systemic racism and discriminatory practices. The meme implicitly invokes this stereotype by suggesting that Blackness (and liberal privilege) led to legal impunity, which reinforces the idea that Black people are inherently more likely to be 'protected' from justice, a harmful and false narrative.",
